  "published": "2026-10-21T18:26:38.25Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.5.1: fixes two cue-layout divergences from chdman. A single-bin multisession cue whose REM LEAD-OUT sits at or before the session's last track (REM LEAD-OUT 00:00:00 is common in real rips) no longer trims that track to a negative length and abort: the frame comparison is now unsigned, exactly like MAME's uint32_t vs int32_t comparison, so chdman's layout is reproduced byte for byte. The CD reader also mirrors chdman's unsigned pad offset, so a pad larger than its track no longer zeroes the track (it reads the source data, as chdman does), including the GD-ROM data/pad/split ordering. Verified byte-identical to chdman createcd on the three reported failure shapes; encoder suite 454/454 and 4214/4214 library tests. Pure C# - zero native dependencies. Targets net8.0/net9.0/net10.0.",
